# MicroDC.ai API key (console.microdc.ai -> API Keys) -- used for embeddings
# and question generation (V2-I), not a judge (this harness doesn't use an
# LLM judge -- see harness/fact_check.py)
MDC_API_KEY=

# Target model ("the chatbot under test") runs locally via Ollama -- must
# match a model already pulled/created with `ollama list`. Required, no
# default: this harness evaluates whatever specific-purpose chatbot you
# point it at, so it won't silently assume one. Example below is our
# current validation subject (BioMistral-7B, chosen because its training
# corpus -- PubMed Central Open Access -- is real, documented, and legally
# reproducible, so the corpus/ directory can hold actual training-data
# excerpts rather than an approximation) -- swap for any other
# domain-specific model without touching code.
# See harness/config.py for details. MicroDC catalog: https://api.microdc.ai/api/public/models
TARGET_MODEL=cniongolo/biomistral

# Generates candidate questions/paraphrases from your corpus (V2-I, see
# generate_questions.py). Deliberately a different model family than
# TARGET_MODEL -- a model shouldn't write its own exam questions.
MDC_GENERATION_MODEL=gpt-oss:120b

# Only needed if Ollama isn't running on the default local port.
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1

# V2-G: if your chatbot isn't served via Ollama or another OpenAI-compatible
# endpoint, point at essentially any REST/JSON API instead by setting
# TARGET_PROVIDER=custom and describing its request/response shape below.
# {{model}}/{{system}}/{{message}} in CUSTOM_REQUEST_TEMPLATE get substituted
# with TARGET_MODEL's value, the grounding system prompt (empty for the
# ungrounded call), and the actual question, respectively.
#
# Worked example, for a hypothetical API that expects
# POST {"bot_id": "...", "sys_ctx": "...", "user_question": "..."}
# and replies {"answer": {"text": "..."}}:
#
# TARGET_PROVIDER=custom
# CUSTOM_ENDPOINT_URL=https://my-chatbot.example.com/api/chat
# CUSTOM_ENDPOINT_HEADERS={"Authorization": "Bearer sk-..."}
# CUSTOM_REQUEST_TEMPLATE={"bot_id": "{{model}}", "sys_ctx": "{{system}}", "user_question": "{{message}}"}
# CUSTOM_RESPONSE_PATH=answer.text